-- title:
--   Drinfeld fibre and linked scalars on the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a natural number $M'$, nonzero, with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume `hι`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ with `hH₁`: $H_1 =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $\cap \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times\big)$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map on units attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`, and the second factor is the kernel of `ZMod.unitsMap` for $\ell \mid q^2M'$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{Laurent}(L)$ with `hK`: $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{Laurent}(L)$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, an $L$-algebra with $L$ as fraction field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$, nonzero, with `hj`: the Laurent series of $j$ is the coefficient embedding of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $\varpi$ be a generator of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`) and $\varpi_t \in A$ a tame constant, `hϖt`: $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two affine charts, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and canonical morphism `ιFin` from $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \mathrm{Spec}\,C$.
--
--   Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin }A\,K\,j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $\iota$nvariants $j_0$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the rigidified Drinfeld-chart package at every supersingular point over $\varpi$, whose clauses are recalled below) asserts: for every point $z$ of $X$, every stalk element $\varpi_z$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin` mapping $y'$ to $z$ and satisfying the same supersingularity condition as $y$, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{W}$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to \mathcal{W}$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}} = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in \mathcal{W}[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = \mathcal{W}[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the ring homomorphism $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ obtained from the germ at $z$ over the image of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$: (i) $e$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — i.e. for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level `GammaH (q^2*M') H₁` and weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficient embedding of $p_f/p_g$, and all $\iota$ with $\iota(\zeta) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$, the $\iota$-image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathtt{conjElemN } q\, \gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k \mathtt{conjElemN } q\, \gamma^{-1}$ — $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if in addition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the restriction of such a $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ as above preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are $\theta \in \mathrm{Aut}(S)$, $c \in \mathcal{W}$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{M}_2(\mathcal{W})$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $\tau$ through $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$, $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the images of $X_0, X_1$, each containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ differ; (vi) for such a prime $P$ containing an element congruent to $X_0$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) a Hasse-type rider: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'$, an exponent $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in \mathcal{W}$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e$ carries the image of this difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   There are then fixed: a point $z$, an element $\varpi_z$ as above with `hϖz`, `hz`, a point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `hy'`, satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y`: $y'$ corresponds to $y$; and a witness package at $z$: a complete discrete valuation domain `W₁`, $\sigma_1 : A \to$ `W₁` with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$, for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts clauses (i)–(vii) above verbatim with these data.
--
--   Further data: an ideal $J$ of $C$ with `hJ`: $J$ is the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ for which there exist $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ with $J'$ the contraction, along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$, of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal generated by the images of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. An $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ with `hB`: $B$ is the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, viewed as an $A$-subalgebra. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ with `hBW`: $B \subseteq W$. The hypothesis `hR1`: $C \le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. The hypothesis `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` (five clauses): for $x \in L$, the image of $x$ lies in $W$ if and only if $x$ comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ if and only if it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\mathfrak{m}_W$, i.e. $f \in W$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of five statements.
--
--   First, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure (that is, every `Algebra (GaloisField q 2) (ResidueField A)` structure) on the residue field $k$ of $A$, there exists a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathtt{drinfeldPoly } q\, k - 1)$ such that: $\rho$ is surjective; $\rho(b) = 0$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; $\rho$ restricted to $A$ is the structure map $k \to$ `CoordRing q k` composed with the residue map of $A$; and for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ for which $W$ is $\tau$-stable ($f \in W \iff \tau f \in W$), there exist a unit $c$ of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ with $(\mathtt{redQ } q\, \gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character sending a pair to the reduction of its determinant times the $(q+1)$-st power of its scalar), such that $\rho(\tau b) = \mathtt{hAction } q\, k\,(\mathtt{redQ } q\,\gamma, c)(\rho b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau b \in B$; such that $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; and such that the same scalar is realised purely scalarly: there exist $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, a level automorphism $\tau'$ at $\gamma'^{-1}$ with $W$ being $\tau'$-stable, and a membership of $(1, c)$ in `hSubgroup q`, with $\rho(\tau' b) = \mathtt{hAction } q\, k\,(1, c)(\rho b)$ for all $b \in B$ with $\tau' b \in B$.
--
--   Second, $B$ is stable under all such level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $f \in B$ implies $\tau f \in B$.
--
--   Third, transitivity on the primes over $\varpi$: for every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$ there exist $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that every $b \in B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ satisfies $\tau b \in B$ and, for any witness of this membership, the resulting element of $B$ lies in $Q$.
--
--   Fourth, a reducedness statement: if $b \in B$ is such that for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ and all witnesses $\tau b \in B$ the element $\tau b$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, then the image of $\varpi$ in $B$ divides $b$.
--
--   Fifth, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$: if $\tau$ preserves $y$, in the sense that for $b \in C$ with $\tau b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $\tau b \in y$, then $W$ is $\tau$-stable, $f \in W \iff \tau f \in W$.
--
--   This is the level-equivariant description of the blow-up chart at a supersingular point of the integral model of a modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$: its special fibre is identified with the Drinfeld coordinate ring over the residue field, the level automorphisms act through the subgroup $\mathrm{hSubgroup}$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$, and the scalar attached to an element of $\Gamma(q)$ is nontrivial and is also realised by a purely scalar level automorphism. It is the variant with a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, valid for an arbitrary prime $q$, and it is used in the assembly of the supersingular affine chart together with its ends, Hasse and inertia data.
